     "type": "text",
     "text": "{\"count\":4,\"rationale\":\"The target is an OR of four collection steps: shareMount, dbReplica, vaultRead and codeRepo. Each one must be cut off. codeRepo needs its own block: either block codeRepo itself, or block both printServer and monitoringHost. Those two are fed almost directly by entry footholds (kerberoast, memoryDump, browserStore, sshKey). fileServer can only be blocked directly, because sshKey comes straight from an entry. So shareMount and dbReplica cannot both be cut with one node, since each also has backupHost, hypervisor or serviceAccount paths. Blocking dbLogin kills vaultRead's parents (localAdmin, hypervisor, secretsManager) but does not cut fileServer or backupHost. No 3-node set covers all four branches. A valid 4-node cut is {apiToken:authenticate, dbLogin:authenticate, fileServer:lateralMovement, codeRepo:collection}. Blocking the four collection steps directly also works.\"}"
    }
   ],
